Z||000022||Master_Sushi||07-13-2001||10:41 AM||||I can get my 88 coupe auto to burn rubber  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. In the winter with its tech wheels and snow tires that is. Only way even then is to let lose around a corner and do a big fishtail. Other then that im limited to parking brake 180's. That dosen't give the same effect, but its still fun, and very smokey. My winter tires will probably only last another season  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. hehe||||reg||14
Z||000023||MoneypitGT||07-13-2001||10:17 PM||||Here is my burnout pic of my '87 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.customdynamix.com/images/blowntran2.jpg"> <BR>Oh wait I mean after my burnout. Time for a motor and tranny swap.<BR>Chris   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects<p>[This message has been edited by MoneypitGT (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000024||California Kid||07-13-2001||10:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MoneypitGT:<BR><B>Here is my burnout pic of my '87 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.customdynamix.com/images/blowntran2.jpg">  <BR>Oh wait I mean after my burnout. Time for a motor and tranny swap.<BR>Chris    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>While I'm sorry to see your busted trans, I think you did a wise thing to post the picture. It should serve as a good reminder that mid-engine cars throw all the weight directly down onto the rear tires. If you have allot of horsepower with big tires, something is going to give sooner or later if you abuse it. It's not wise to do a "dry" burnout in these cars, if you really, really want to do it, put down some water or oil the tires up. Actually I'm surprised you didn't take out the short axle or CV Joint, they generally break before the trans lets loose. Speaking from experience......part of the learning curve !!! Hope you get your car back together soon!<BR>Tom||||reg||1
Z||000025||lowCG||07-14-2001||04:26 PM||||Yeah,I don't do burnouts very often myself,the idea of working on my back in a pool of gear oil just doesn't appeal to me.<BR>My subframe is stressed to the point of cracking around the motor mounts without doing any burnouts,had it all welded,reinforced,and braced.||||reg||1
